From b20a8657c3ecc5b66c04a5c94a6c7cafa5a2a010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:04:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a gateway restart's drain no longer kills or
 charges the Kanban runs it waits on [daveey]

2026-10-30, hub and example-laptop: a core update restarted each gateway with managed Kanban
runs in flight (hub 11, Mac 5+3). The restart's after-turn wait (cap 1800 s) refused
the submitters' redials as draining/restart_wait/update_paused. Each submitter treated
that as owner silence and gave up at OWNER_WAIT_S (180 s), its exit made
_watch_submitter end the very turn the drain was waiting on (Managed worker lost:
EOFError), and the dead-worker sweep (live waitpid, or the next gateway reading the log
trailer) booked identical crashes: systemic, gave_up to triage on the first failure.

Worker (kanban_worker_client):
- A draining/starting answer (GatewayUnavailableError in _TRANSIENT_OWNER_STATES,
  including restart_wait and update_paused, or GatewayRPCError runtime_draining/retired)
  counts as an owner answer, up to the owner's own agent.restart_after_turn_timeout.
  Real silence still fails after OWNER_WAIT_S. A continuous drain ends the worker at
  cap + OWNER_WAIT_S.
- After the owner restarted, giving up (or reading an "unknown" receipt) raises
  OwnerRestartLost and the worker exits KANBAN_OWNER_RESTART_EXIT_CODE (69).

Dispatcher:
- Exit 69 (reaped or read from the trailer) is kind owner_restart. The run is booked
  outcome "reclaimed" (metadata owner_restart: true) with ONE "owner_restart_lost"
  event. The card goes back to ready with consecutive_failures unchanged, and the
  systemic crash tally skips it.
- check_respawn_guard spaces the respawn (owner_restart_cooldown, 120 s,
  HERMES_KANBAN_OWNER_RESTART_COOLDOWN_SECONDS). _protocol_violation_streak skips the run.

Tests: test_kanban_worker_owner_restart.py (RED before the fix: 13 of 15), plus the
silence and restart-wait tests that change meaning. The handoff E2E releases the held
turn 210 s into the update's drain, and the head column asserts the in-flight run
completes in one run.
